@igordayen On the integration tests: they were not run here. There is no Gemini API key and no Vertex application-default credentials in this environment, so `GoogleGenAiChatIntegrationIT`, `GoogleGenAiAllModelsIT`, `GoogleGenAiEmbeddingIT` and `GoogleGenAiToolResponseIT` stay disabled (they need `GEMINI_API_KEY`), and so does `BlankTurnRePromptIT` (it needs Vertex credentials plus `GOOGLE_PROJECT_ID` and `EMBABEL_RUN_VERTEX_INTEGRATION_TESTS`). The green fork build runs `mvn -U -B test verify` without the `integration-tests` profile, so it is not evidence that those classes executed.

What is covered: the unit tests in the module, which exercise the thinking opt-out path. If you can run the `integration-tests` profile for `embabel-agent-google-genai-autoconfigure` with your credentials, that would settle it. If they fail, I'll fix the branch. If you'd rather not take the change without a live run from my side, I'm fine with closing it.

(Prepared with the assistance of an AI coding agent.)
